From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:39:37 +0900
Subject: Disks plugin: mounted file systems from mountinfo when Solid finds
 no volumes

In a container without udev, UDisks2 or /dev nodes for the disks Solid lists no storage volumes,
so there were no disk/<id>/* sensors and disk/all/* stayed empty: System Monitor's Overview said
"This page is missing some sensors" for its Disks face and the Disk Usage widget had nothing to
show (docs/104). When Solid yields no volume the plugin now
takes the file systems on block devices from /proc/self/mountinfo: pseudo file systems, tmpfs,
FUSE and overlays are left out, as are read-only images; a device mounted at several places (the
data partition bind mounted many times) counts once, at "/", a whole-file-system mount, the
mount holding the home folder or the shortest. The id is the device-mapper name ("rungic-root",
"userdata"; stable across boots, unlike dm-N) or the kernel name; the name is "System" for /,
"Home" for the volume of the home folder, otherwise the mount point (zh_CN translated). Sizes come
from statvfs, read and write rates from /proc/diskstats as before. Parsing and selection in
MountInfo with tests (mountinfotest, fixtures from the Rungic container and a btrfs desktop).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic for containers without udev; check upstream master first]
X-Rungic-Tests: L1:mountinfotest
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/104
